        "original_id": "87973b45-9751-5ef7-9659-4db98cbecf5f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Bacon, Lawrence Turman, Curtis Hanson, Meryl Streep, David Strathairn, John C. Reilly, Benjamin Bratt, Joseph Mazzello\n- Films: The River Wild, Footloose, JFK, A Few Good Men, Apollo 13, Mystic River, Pretty Poison, The Great White Hope, The Thing, Mass Appeal, Short Circuit, American History X\n- Roles: actor, musician, director, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Lawrence Turman produced the films Pretty Poison (1968) and The Great White Hope (1970).\n- Lawrence Turman produced The Thing (1982), Mass Appeal (1984), and Short Circuit (1986).\n- Kevin Norwood Bacon was born on July 8, 1958, and he is an American actor and musician.\n- Kevin Bacon had notable film roles in Footloose (1984), JFK (1991), and A Few Good Men (1992).\n- The River Wild is a 1994 American adventure crime-thriller film directed by Curtis Hanson.\n- The River Wild stars Meryl Streep, Kevin Bacon, David Strathairn, John C. Reilly, Benjamin Bratt, and Joseph Mazzello as Roarke.\n- Lawrence Turman produced The River Wild (1994) and American History X (1998).\n- Kevin Bacon had notable film roles in Apollo 13 (1995) and Mystic River (2003).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
